    "report": {
      "assessment_status": "completed",
      "conclusion": "partial",
      "summary": "Re-checked with fresh queries, the alert condition still reproduces: in the 5-minute window ending 2026-10-15T18:33:53Z, checkout's oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder SPAN_KIND_SERVER spans were 16.25 ERROR and 0 STATUS_CODE_UNSET (ratio 1.0), and the sliding 300 s series at 60 s steps shows errors climbing 1.25, 5, 7.5, 15.0, 17.5, 16.25 while non-error spans fell 20, 15, 6.25, 1.25, 0, 0. On your follow-up: (1) card-type isolation cannot be answered, because no telemetry returned in this Run carries a card-brand/type dimension — payment's transaction metric exposes only app_payment_currency (CAD, USD) cohorts, and the trace projection shows only status tags plus clipped error fields, whose only visible request attribute is 'app.loyalty.level=gold'. What can be said is that the failure is currently total for observed traffic rather than a partial subset: over 18:28:53Z-18:33:53Z checkout made 16.2518 Charge client calls with rpc_grpc_status_code=2 and 0 with code 0 (OK), whereas over 18:23:53Z-18:28:53Z it made 20.00 OK against 1.25 failing, so roughly 20 of 21 charges succeeded in the preceding window and none in the trailing window; both observable currency cohorts are simultaneously unchanged (CAD 1230, USD 9992 at every 60 s sample across the trailing 5 minutes). (2) All charges fail at payment's own token check with one identical signature: 'Payment request failed. Invalid token. app.loyalty.level=gold' raised at module.exports.charge (/usr/src/app/charge.js:37:13) via chargeServiceHandler (/usr/src/app/index.js:21:22), surfaced to checkout as gRPC 13 and to the frontends as HTTP 500; three sampled traces in 18:31-18:33Z and one at 18:06:47Z carry the same message and stack. (3) Of the previous incident's six checks, three apply and reproduce here (fine-step error/unset ratio, client-RPC breakdown showing only oteldemo.PaymentService non-zero, and payment's own Charge ratio matching checkout's PlaceOrder ratio); the earlier-episode signature check is only partly satisfied (identical signature sampled, no duration baseline); the log/configuration/card-token check and the deployment replica check cannot be applied because no log, configuration, feature-flag or replica evidence exists in this Run. The 24 h view shows a rare, concentrated pattern: ERROR PlaceOrder server spans were non-zero at only three 1 h evaluation instants (24.41, 7.12, 36.61) and the alert hour as a whole was about 23% errors (36.61 ERROR vs 121.02 non-error), so the alert is driven by the short trailing window over a small absolute count. Why payment rejects the token, and whether it is card-type-specific, remain unknown."
    }
  },
